\title{Soundness Notions}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Which soundness a theorem is about determines whether it survives the [Fiat–Shamir transform](dhsorens-002G). A table of the notions, the implications between them, and which compilation step preserves each belongs on this page.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Soundness, knowledge soundness, special soundness — and the implications between them.}
        \li{Round-by-round soundness and state-restoration soundness: what they demand, and why they were invented.}
        \li{Soundness error versus security level in bits; how error accumulates across rounds, queries, and repetitions.}
        \li{Provable versus conjectured soundness, and which deployed parameters rest on which. See [proximity gaps](dhsorens-002P).}
        \li{What "128-bit security" means for a hash-based system once [grinding](dhsorens-003A) is counted.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: [How to Prove False Statements](https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/118) for why the distinctions are not academic.
}
